vanilla.ponder.tag.redstone=Redstone
vanilla.ponder.tag.redstone.description=Components which help with redstone engineering
vanilla.ponder.redstone_lamp.header=Redstone Lamp
vanilla.ponder.redstone_lamp.text_1=Redstone Lamps stay dark on their own and light up as soon as they receive a redstone signal
vanilla.ponder.redstone_lamp.text_2=An active power source or a powered block next to the lamp lights it directly
vanilla.ponder.redstone_lamp.text_3=Redstone Dust, Repeaters and Comparators pointing into the lamp light it too, including dust on top of it
vanilla.ponder.redstone_lamp_delay.header=Redstone Lamp Timing
vanilla.ponder.redstone_lamp_delay.text_1=Once the signal is gone, the lamp takes 4 game ticks to turn off. It conducts redstone, so a powered lamp can drive adjacent components
vanilla.ponder.piston.header=Pistons
vanilla.ponder.piston.text_1=A piston pushes the block in front of it up to 12 blocks, as long as the row is not blocked
vanilla.ponder.piston.text_2=A sticky piston pulls the block back with it. Slime and honey blocks carry their neighbours along too
vanilla.ponder.inputs.header=Levers and Buttons
vanilla.ponder.inputs.text_1=A lever stays on until it is used again, and keeps powering whatever is next to it
vanilla.ponder.inputs.text_2=A button gives a short pulse: stone buttons last 10 ticks, wooden ones 15, and an arrow hitting a wooden button sets it off too
vanilla.ponder.repeater.header=Redstone Repeater
vanilla.ponder.repeater.text_1=A repeater passes a signal in one direction only, and refreshes it back to full strength
vanilla.ponder.repeater.text_2=Using it adds a delay of 1, 2, 3 or 4 ticks. Locking it with another repeater from the side freezes it in place
vanilla.ponder.comparator.header=Redstone Comparator
vanilla.ponder.comparator.text_1=A comparator reads the container behind it and outputs a signal from 0 to 15 depending on how full it is
vanilla.ponder.comparator.text_2=Using it switches to subtract mode, where the output is the rear signal minus the stronger of the two side signals
vanilla.ponder.hopper.header=Hopper
vanilla.ponder.hopper.text_1=A hopper pulls items in from above and pushes them into the container it points at
vanilla.ponder.hopper.text_2=It moves one item every 8 ticks. Powering it with redstone stops it until the signal goes away
vanilla.ponder.tag.mining=Mining
vanilla.ponder.tag.mining.description=Ways to break blocks and gather what they drop
vanilla.ponder.shared.drops=Once broken, the block drops %1$s
vanilla.ponder.mining.header=Mining Ores
vanilla.ponder.mining.text_1=Iron ore needs a stone pickaxe or better. Mined with anything weaker, it drops nothing
vanilla.ponder.moss.header=Spreading Moss
vanilla.ponder.moss.text_1=Bone meal on a moss block turns stone, dirt and similar blocks around it into moss
vanilla.ponder.tnt.header=TNT
vanilla.ponder.tnt.text_1=Flint and steel, fire or a redstone signal lights TNT. It hops up and explodes 4 seconds later
vanilla.ponder.tnt.text_2=The blast breaks the blocks around it, and only some of them drop as items
vanilla.ponder.lever_tnt.header=Lighting TNT with Redstone
vanilla.ponder.lever_tnt.text_1=A lever, or any other signal reaching the TNT, lights it as well
